gpu_work_summary (on, hot reload): every 10 seconds the D3D12 command processor logs its swaps per second, the draws,
resolves and submissions per swap and the time it was blocked on the GPU fence and on the async submission thread
(GPU-bound or CPU-bound). It also logs the EDRAM render targets with the most drawn pixels (largest viewport, guest
and host size, draws per swap, share of pixels), the resolves by source pitch and destination texture size, and the
swap packet, front buffer texture and presenter input sizes. The presenter logs its input, output and swap chain
sizes and the effect chain whenever they change.

